# um-texts 1
=== MATERIAL Adamantium
Adamantite
Very good material for weapons and armor.

=== MATERIAL Bronze
Bronze
The cheapest and softest metal for making weapons.

=== MATERIAL Burned_bones
Hard bone
Weapons made of hard bone are sharper and stronger than those made of thick bone alone.

=== MATERIAL Cotton
Cotton
Cotton is more expensive than regular fabric, but it looks better.

=== MATERIAL Decayed_bones
Thin bone
It's easy to get this kind of material, but virtually impossible to make a decent weapon out of it.

=== MATERIAL Diamond
Diamond
Only the best craftsmen of a now extinct race knew the secret of working this material.

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Black
Rawhide of the blue dragon
This dragon scales are used to make strong leather armor, providing good protection against lightning.

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Black_Bones
Blue Dragon Bone
The perfect material for a bone weapon! But it is very hard to get...

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Green
Green dragon rawhide
This dragon scales are used to make strong leather armor, providing good protection against acid.

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Green_Bones
Green dragon bone
A nearly perfect material for bone weapons.

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Red
Rawhide of the red dragon
This dragon scales are used to make strong leather armor, providing good protection against fire.

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Red_Bones
Red Dragon Bone
Very good material for bone weapons.

=== MATERIAL Dry_bones
Thick bone
Weapons made of thick bones can be sharpened better than those made of skinny bones.

=== MATERIAL Granite
Granite
A heavier and nicer material than regular stone. Weapons made of granite are also better than those made of ordinary stone.

=== MATERIAL Iron
Iron
Iron is better than bronze, but worse than other metals.

=== MATERIAL Lizard_Black
The skin of a mountain lizard
Expensive, durable and secure.

=== MATERIAL Lizard_Blue
The skin of the lake lizard
You can make good armor out of this kind of skin.

=== MATERIAL Lizard_Green
Forest Lizard skin
Not a very durable leather, but also inexpensive.

=== MATERIAL Malachite
Obsidian
The best material for stone weapons, capable of carrying powerful spells.

=== MATERIAL Meteoric
Meteorite
The most durable metal, the best material for weapons and armor.

=== MATERIAL Mithrill
Mitrile
Very lightweight and very strong. Mithril items can store powerful spells within them.

=== MATERIAL Ogre
Ogre skin
Ogres never part with a skin like this... in their lifetime.

